 Therefore, the nth Fibonacci number can be found by raising the transformation matrix M = [[1, 1], [1, 0]] to the power of (n-1). The resulting matrix will yield F(n) in the top-left corner. 

 You can implement the matrix exponentiation using the exponentiation by squaring technique. Here's a brief pseudocode overview: 

